// @@@ For every valid index 'i' that is greater than or equal to the current index and less than the old size of the list, the new element at position 'i+1' is equal to the old element at position 'i'. This implies that all the elements in the list after the inserted index remain the same as they were before the operation.

--------------------
// @@@ For any index 'i' such that 'index' is less than or equal to 'i' and 'i' is less than the old size of the list, the next element in the list after the index 'i' is null and the previous element at 'i' is null or equal to the previous element in the old list.

--------------------
// @@@ The attribute at the inserted index and all the attributes after it remain the same as before the insertion.

